issue.body:
If the [GeoIP processor](https://www.elastic.co/guide/en/elasticsearch/reference/master/geoip-processor.html) is not configured correctly or if it can not connect to Elastic's GeoIP's endpoint for 30 days the processor will start emitting `tags` under `_source`. 

> If your cluster can’t connect to the Elastic GeoIP endpoint or you want to manage your own updates, see [Manage your own GeoIP2 database updates](https://www.elastic.co/guide/en/elasticsearch/reference/master/geoip-processor.html#manage-geoip-database-updates).

> If Elasticsearch can’t connect to the endpoint for 30 days all updated databases will become invalid. Elasticsearch will stop enriching documents with geoip data and will add tags: ["_geoip_expired_database"] field instead.


Currently our mappings are strict and will start rejecting documents if the `geoip` processor acts up and inject `tags`.


e.g


```json
POST metrics-apm.internal-default/_doc?pipeline=metrics-apm.internal-8.1.0
{
    "@timestamp": "2022-03-04T12:33:00.000Z",
  "observer": {
    "version": "8.1.0",
    "version_major": 8
  }
}
```
*`metrics-apm.internal-8.1.0` is the default pipeline*

will return: 

```json
{
  "error" : {
    "root_cause" : [
      {
        "type" : "strict_dynamic_mapping_exception",
        "reason" : "mapping set to strict, dynamic introduction of [tags] within [_doc] is not allowed"
      }
    ],
    "type" : "strict_dynamic_mapping_exception",
    "reason" : "mapping set to strict, dynamic introduction of [tags] within [_doc] is not allowed"
  },
  "status" : 400
}
```

Tested on `8.1.0-SNAPSOT` but likely not version bound.
